# Wall-clock ceiling for the pull-request pipeline. R1085-16 item 5 requires
# this to be recorded and enforced. `scripts/check-ci-wall-clock.rs` discovers
# all PR-triggered workflows, computes each workflow's critical path through the
# needs: DAG weighted by timeout-minutes, recurses into reusable workflows, and
# verifies that the discovered maximum equals measured_minutes and does not
# exceed ceiling_minutes.
#
# Discovery result (2026-10-08):
#   issue-1028-agent-ladder.yml: 225 min
#     plan(30m) -> ladder(135m) -> leaf-evidence(15m) -> composites(30m) -> compare(15m)
#   release.yml: 140 min
#     detect-changes(5m) -> build-artifacts(20m) -> test(90m)
#       -> build(20m) -> pipeline-status(5m)
#
# The ladder's all-mode corpus is split into 31 independent primary legs and
# 16 single-composite legs consuming validated current-run leaf artifacts.
# Its static backstops sum to 225 minutes; cold all-mode timings still have to
# establish whether every primary leg can retire its recorded exception.
#
# Push-only jobs (auto-release, manual-release, build-pages, deploy-pages,
# changelog-pr) and workflow_dispatch-only jobs (manual-release, changelog-pr)
# are excluded from the critical path by the check script.
ci_wall_clock pull_request_pipeline
  measured_minutes 225
  measured_date "2026-10-08"
  ceiling_minutes 225
  workflow ".github/workflows/issue-1028-agent-ladder.yml"
  chain "plan(30m)->ladder(135m)->leaf-evidence(15m)->composites(30m)->compare(15m)"
  note "The all-mode ladder preserves all 63 nodes across 31 primary legs and 16 artifact-fed composites. Its static DAG remains 225 minutes: plan 30 + primary 135 + validated leaf join15 + composite30 + compare 15. This ceiling is a backstop, not an observed runtime; actual cold all-mode measurements are required before retiring the primary exception. PR depth-five uses 16 independent leaf-pair legs and skips the composite wave."
  requirement "R1085-16"
